# Specific magic armor and shields
# Source: The (mostly) Complete Dragon Magazine Compendium - Magic Items (compendium pp. 1420-1595).
# DESC ends with the original Dragon/Dungeon Magazine issue and article. SOURCEPAGE = compendium PDF page.
# SPROP summarizes aura, caster level, body slot, activation and item level.

Agustinius's Folly	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfHeavy.ArmorType_Heavy.Armor.Heavy.Suit.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Banded Mail	ACCHECK:-6	MAXDEX:1	SPELLFAILURE:35	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|6|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|6	COST:6000	WT:35	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1423	SPROP:Aura Moderate enchantment; CL 8th; Slot Body; Activation Full (command) and Free; Item level 10	DESC:This +2 banded mail grants its wearer the ability to inspire courage once per day as an 8th-level bard. To activate the ability, the wearer must use a full-round action to give an inspiring speech. The ability lasts for as long as the wearer keeps speaking (which is a free action) +5 rounds. Unfortunately, the magic of this armor is unstable, and 10%% of the time, the ability does not work and instead panics all affected creatures for 10 rounds. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, creator must be a bard. [Dragon #324 (Magic Shop: Power At A Price)]
Arboreal Armor	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfLight.ArmorType_Light.Armor.Light.Suit.Nonmetal.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Leather	ACCHECK:0	MAXDEX:6	SPELLFAILURE:10	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|0	COST:16000	WT:15	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	BONUS:SKILL|Hide|4	SOURCEPAGE:p.1423	SPROP:Aura Faint abjuration; CL 5th; Slot Body; Activation –– and Standard (command); Item level 14	DESC:Arboreal armor appears as plates of bark held together by vines and covered with patches of moss. The armor has an earthy smell, and it is favored by wood elves, who find it especially suited to their naturalistic taste. &nl;Druids created arboreal armor for their ranger allies so they might better defend the wilds against despoilers. Arboreal armor functions as a set of +2 leather armor. Its appearance gives the wearer a +4 bonus on Hide checks made in forested settings. The armor automatically regenerates damage dealt to it at the rate of 1 hit point per hour. The wearer can cast entangle three times per day, and the armor itself casts goodberry every morning at dawn, growing five berries from its own form. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, entangle, goodberry. [Dragon #326 (Magic Shop: Nature Unleashed)]
Armor of the Long Journey	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfHeavy.ArmorType_Heavy.Armor.Heavy.Suit.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Full Plate	ACCHECK:-6	MAXDEX:1	SPELLFAILURE:35	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|8|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|6	COST:39650	WT:25	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1423	SPROP:Aura Moderate abjuration; CL 6th; Slot Body; Item level 17	DESC:A suit of armor of the long journey is made from a mundane-looking steel alloy bearing no special marks or runes. While the armor appears bulky, a closer inspection reveals that it is actually as light as a chain shirt. Armor of the long journey protects its &nl;wearer as a suit of +2 full plate armor of cold resistance. The suit, however, is so light that its owner can move at his normal base land speed, rather than the reduced land speed caused by normal full plate. The armor of the long journey also aids its wearer in carrying great loads. While wearing this armor, the owner treats all medium loads as light loads, and all heavy loads as medium loads. Furthermore, the wearer of armor of the long journey never suffers from the effects of fatigue caused by traveling. Combat and other conditions (such as swimming, raging, and certain spells) fatigue the wearer normally. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, bear's endurance, resist energy. [Dragon #328 (Bazaar of the Bizarre: Treasures of the Elven Empire)]
Armor of the Woodland	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfLight.ArmorType_Light.Armor.Light.Suit.Nonmetal.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Leather	ACCHECK:0	MAXDEX:6	SPELLFAILURE:10	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|0	COST:75755	WT:1	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|3|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1423	SPROP:Aura Moderate conjuration; CL 9th; Slot Body; Activation –– and Standard (command); Item level 19	DESC:The armor, which is almost as light as a wool shirt, looks like a jumbled pile of crushed leaves, broken branches, and thin pieces of bark. &nl;Shaped in the form of a leather vest, a suit of armor of the woodland comes complete with shoulder pads, elbow protectors, and greaves. The most common of these suits are of a dark green color, but shades can vary from bright reds and oranges to pale yellows and greens. Armor of the woodland is a suit of +3 leather armor. Whenever the wearer of such a suit of armor travels through a forest, he adds 10 feet to his base land speed and gains the trackless step ability of druids. The armor's most impressive power allows its wearer to enter trees and magically transport from one to another three times per day. This ability works just like the tree stride spell as cast by a 9th-level druid. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, woodland stride ability or pass without trace, tree stride. [Dragon #322(Sneaky, Stealthy, & Stylish: New Magic Items for Assassins, Rogues, and Bards)]
Armor of Thror	TYPE:Magic.ArmorProfHeavy.ArmorType_Heavy.Armor.Heavy.Suit.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Half-Plate	ACCHECK:-7	MAXDEX:0	SPELLFAILURE:40	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|7|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|7	COST:60750	WT:50	SOURCEPAGE:p.1424	SPROP:Aura Strong abjuration; CL 13th; Slot Body; Item level 18	DESC:This armor is a set of beautifully crafted half-plate. Fashioned from solid gold with many intricate patterns etched into the metal, these suits hold Thror's heraldic symbol upon the breastplate: the face of a mighty boar holding a rose between its clenched teeth. Although most people do not recognize this ancient and prestigious symbol, many dwarves do. An armor of Thror is a +2 fortification (heavy) half-plate. In addition, if an enemy makes a melee attack that would normally cause a critical hit or sneak attack, the armor strikes that foe with a bolt of energy that deals 8d6 points of electricity damage. An attacker who makes a DC 14 Reflex save suffers only half damage. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, lightning bolt. [Dragon #323 (Magic Shop: Treasures of the Dwarven Holds)]
Arms of House Melarn	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfMedium.ArmorType_Medium.Armor.Medium.Suit.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Chainmail	ACCHECK:-5	MAXDEX:2	SPELLFAILURE:30	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|5|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|5	COST:85300	WT:20	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|5|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	BONUS:STAT|STR|4|TYPE=Enhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1424	SPROP:Aura Strong transmutation; CL 12th; Slot Body; Item level 20	DESC:This armor is a suit of +5 elven chainmail of nimbleness that also grants the wearer a +4 enhancement bonus to Strength. The nimbleness property raises the maximum Dexterity bonus of the armor to +6 and reduces the armor check penalty to -1. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, bull's strength, cat's grace. [Dragon #312 (Rogues Gallery: The Heroes of the War of the Spider Queen Part II)]
Arms of the Jaezred Chaulssin	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfLight.ArmorType_Light.Armor.Light.Suit.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Chain Shirt	ACCHECK:-2	MAXDEX:4	SPELLFAILURE:20	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|4|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|2	COST:92250	WT:10	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|4|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	BONUS:SKILL|Hide|5|TYPE=Circumstance	BONUS:SAVE|Fortitude,Reflex,Will|3|TYPE=Luck	SOURCEPAGE:p.1424	SPROP:Aura Strong transmutation; CL 12th; Slot Body; Item level 20	DESC:This excellent armor is a suit of +4 mithral blueshine chain shirt of nimbleness. The nimbleness property increases the mithral chain shirt's maximum Dexterity bonus to +8; the blueshine property renders the armor (but not necessarily the wearer) immune to acid and rust attacks and confers a +5 circumstance bonus on Hide checks. Finally, the wearer of the arms of the Jaezred Chaulssin gains a +3 luck bonus on all saving throws. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, cat's grace, resistance, 5 ranks in Craft (alchemy). [Dragon #322 (Heroes of the War of the Spider Queen Part III)]
Battleplate	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfMedium.ArmorType_Medium.Armor.Medium.Suit.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Breastplate	ACCHECK:-4	MAXDEX:3	SPELLFAILURE:25	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|5|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|4	COST:31050	WT:30	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1424	SPROP:Aura Moderate transmutation; CL 9th; Slot Body; Activation –– and Standard (command); Item level 16	DESC:Otherwise unremarkable in appearance, an etching of a wide maple tree with golden leaves decorates this armor's glistening silver breastplate. &nl;A suit of battleplate is a +2 mithral breastplate of improved silent moves. The armor bears a glamour that allows its wearer to change the battleplate's appearance to that of a simple tunic, making it possible to wear the armor in a populated area without rousing suspicions. Finally, in addition to the Move Silently bonus granted by the armor's improved silent moves, battleplate grants its wearer a +5 competence bonus on Jump and Tumble checks. Because its mithral construction makes battleplate light armor, bards can cast spells while wearing it without the risk of arcane spell failure. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, Still Spell, disguise self, jump, silence. [Dragon #333 (Bazaar of the Bizarre: Treasures of the Gnome Hills)]
Breastplate of Hardiness	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfMedium.ArmorType_Medium.Armor.Medium.Suit.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Breastplate	ACCHECK:-4	MAXDEX:3	SPELLFAILURE:25	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|5|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|4	COST:43350	WT:30	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|3|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1424	SPROP:Aura Strong abjuration; CL 9th; Slot Body; Item level 17	DESC:A breastplate of hardiness is a blood-red +3 fire resistance breastplate that grants its wearer a number of temporary hit points equal to his Constitution score. Whenever the wearer of a breastplate of hardiness takes damage, subtract the armor's temporary hit points first. Once the amount of temporary hit points drops to 0, the wearer takes damage as normal. A breastplate of hardiness regenerates lost temporary hit point at a rate of 1 per hour until all of its temporary hit points are available again. The armor grants a wearer temporary hit points as long as the armor is worn, and the hit points vanish if the armor is removed. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, bear's endurance, resist energy. [Dragon #323 (Magic Shop: Treasures of the Dwarven Holds)]
Fedor's Shield	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ShieldProfHeavy.Shield.Heavy.ShieldProf.Specific	PROFICIENCY:SHIELD|Shield (Heavy)	ACCHECK:-2	CRITMULT:x2	CRITRANGE:1	DAMAGE:1d4	WIELD:OneHanded	SIZE:M	SPELLFAILURE:15	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=Shield	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|2	COST:16157	WT:2	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=ShieldEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1424	SPROP:Aura Moderate transmutation; CL 8th; Slot –– (held); Item level 14	DESC:This simple-looking round burgundy-colored shield bears a large white star emblazed upon it. A battered metal disk in the center of the star reinforces the lightwood shield. Although simple in its design, a closer look at Fedor's shield reveals its masterwork quality as well as its remarkable lightness. The scent of freshly cut lightwood also lingers around the item, regardless of its age. &nl;This beautiful and surprisingly light large shield grants stability to anyone who carries it. Fedor's shield is a +2 heavy wooden shield of bashing, but the item only weights 2 pounds and confers no armor check penalty. Furthermore, if you have heavy shield proficiency, you gain a +4 bonus on checks made to resist being bull rushed or tripped whenever you wield Fedor's shield. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, bull's strength, levitate. &nl;Cost to Create: 8,157 gp, 646 XP, 16 days. &nl;Lore: Few of the shields fashioned by Fedor remain, and those original items frequently sell for as much as four times their actual value as magic items when sold to collectors. Weaponsmiths and armorers long ago uncovered how to make copies of Fedor's famous shield, and these copies are not uncommon— especially on the high plains. [Dragon #349 (Web Supplement: The Horde – Barbarians of the Endless Waste)]
The Fool's Plate	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ShieldProf.Shield.Buckler.ShieldProfBuckler.Specific	PROFICIENCY:SHIELD|Buckler	ACCHECK:-1	SPELLFAILURE:5	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1|TYPE=Shield	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|1	COST:7200	WT:3	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1|TYPE=ShieldEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1425	SPROP:Aura Faint illusion; CL 3rd; Slot –– (held); Activation –– and Standard (command); Item level 11	DESC:At first glance, this item appears to be nothing more than a silver platter. &nl;When used as a buckler, it acts like a +1 buckler and its mirrored face forces anyone who attacks the wielder to make a DC 10 Will save or come under the effect of a daze spell. The wielder can also use the shield once per day to cast hypnotic pattern. Unfortunately, whenever either of these spells are invoked, the shield's user must make the same save as his target or be affected by the same effect. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, daze, hypnotic pattern. [Dragon #324 (Magic Shop: Power At A Price)]
Ice Armor of the Northlands	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfHeavy.ArmorType_Heavy.Armor.Heavy.Suit.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Full Plate	ACCHECK:-6	MAXDEX:1	SPELLFAILURE:35	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|8|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|6	COST:58650	WT:100	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1425	SPROP:Aura Moderate evocation; CL 7th; Slot Body; Item level 18	DESC:This full plate armor is ice-blue and shrouded in frost. The interior is lined with thick fur. When worn, it exudes an extremely cold white mist. &nl;The armor of the northlands wreathes you in a supernatural icy mist that deals cold damage to nearby creatures. Ice armor of the northlands is +1 full plate that wreathes you in a supernatural icy mist at all times that deals 2d6 points of cold damage each round to all creatures within 10 feet of you (if Large or larger) or to all creatures within 5 feet of you (if Medium or smaller). The armor deals the same damage to you each round. Fire giants have also realized the potential for this armor, and thus variants that wreathe the wearer in flames and deal fire damage instead of cold damage exist. Characters can resize Large armor to fit a Medium wearer by succeeding at a DC 20 Craft (armorsmithing) check. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, fire shield. &nl;Lore: A DC 20 Knowledge (arcana) or Knowledge (history) check provides the following information. Brynja Skjaldvör, the infamous frost giantess, crafted the first ice armor of the northlands for herself jealously guarding the secret of its creation. With her fearsome warbands in tow she scourged the northlands, conquering settlement after settlement. The bards of the northlands sing forlorn tales of her cruelty, noting her ferociousness in battle and her legendary freezing armor. [Dragon #345 (Bazaar of the Bizarre: For and Against The Giants)]
Quaal's Surreptitious Armor of Expedience	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ArmorProfLight.ArmorType_Light.Armor.Light.Suit.Specific	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Chain Shirt	ACCHECK:-2	MAXDEX:4	SPELLFAILURE:20	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|4|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|2	COST:65250	WT:12.5	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|4|TYPE=ArmorEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1425	SPROP:Aura Strong transmutation; CL 12th; Slot Torso; Activation Standard (command); Item level 19	DESC:Dark feathers and a rabbit's foot hanging near the waist adorn this mithral rune-etched chain shirt. &nl;This +4 twilight mobility mithral chain shirt (+8 armor bonus; armor check penalty of -1) completely negates its arcane spell failure chance. Mithral and the twilight ability of this armor reduces its armor check penalty to 0%% while the mobility ability grants you the benefit of the Mobility feat even if you do not meet the prerequisite. In addition, you gain the ability to cast fly and longstrider as spell-like abilities once each per day. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, cat's grace, fly, longstrider. &nl;Cost to Create: 33,250 gp, 2,560 XP. &nl;Lore: Quaal learned the craft of magic late in his career, but he never lost the desire to draw his sword and enter the fray. To maximize his mobility and the cast spells in melee he crafted this piece of armor. [Dragon #359 (Treasures of Greyhawk: Magic of the Company of Seven)]
Rune Armor	TYPE:Magic.ArmorProfMedium.ArmorType_Medium.Armor.Medium.Suit.Specific.Artifact.Minor	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Breastplate	ACCHECK:-4	MAXDEX:3	SPELLFAILURE:25	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|5|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|4	COST:0	WT:15	SOURCEPAGE:p.1425	SPROP:Aura Strong abjuration, divination, illusion, necromancy, and transmutation; CL 20th; Slot Body; Activation –– and Free	DESC:This suit of armor appears to have been cobbled together from several different types of armor. The components all appear corroded and old, but on each piece glows an inset rune. Each rune has a unique shape and color, and a corresponding power usable by the armor's occupant. &nl;The armor itself functions as a mithral breastplate +4. Activating one of the runes on the armor is a free action, although only one rune may be activated per round. Once activated, a rune's power remains active for 10 rounds. Only two runes can be active at any given time, and each rune can only be activated up to 3 times before they become dormant. A dormant rune can be awakened by applying a specific potion or magic oil that has been enhanced by an obscure alchemical catalyst invented long ago by Bersteck Maure. A dose of rune catalyst is worth 500 gp and has no additional powers of its own–the exact formula for creating this silvery liquid is known to Bersteck Maure and few others. Currently, each rune has only one activation remaining before it needs to be wakened again. The powers of the runes (and the potion required to awaken them) are as follows. Hoof (Black, oil of magic vestment): Grants DR 10/magic and immunity to bull rush, tripping, and overrun attempts. Claw (Green, oil of keen edge): Any slashing or piercing weapons currently wielded gain keen edge and are poisoned with black lotus extract (Fort DC 20, 3d6 Con/3d6 Con). Sword (Silver, oil of greater magic weapon): Any weapon currently wielded gains a +5 enhancement bonus. The wielder cannot be disarmed. Shield (Blue, potion of displacement): Grants a +4 deflection bonus to AC and displacement (50%% miss chance). Wing (Gold, potion of fly): Grants a 60 ft. fly speed (perfect). Eye (Red, potion of arcane sight): Protects the wearer from blindness and grants the ability to see invisibility and arcane sight. [Dungeon #139 (Castle Maure: The Greater Halls)]
Shield of Obstruction	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ShieldProfLight.Shield.Light.ShieldProf.Specific	PROFICIENCY:SHIELD|Shield (Light)	ACCHECK:-1	CRITMULT:x2	CRITRANGE:1	DAMAGE:1d3	WIELD:Light	SIZE:M	SPELLFAILURE:5	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1|TYPE=Shield	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|1	COST:27403	WT:5	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|3|TYPE=ShieldEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1426	SPROP:Aura Moderate transmutation; CL 9th; Slot –– (held); Activation Standard (command); Item level 16	DESC:Shields of obstruction are spiked light wooden shields most commonly shaped into the form of pointed-edged leaves. Along with countless battle scars, each is covered with intricate carvings of vines that bristle with protruding thorns. This tangled motif often circles the ancient insignia of the elven house the shield's original owner served. &nl;A shield of obstruction is a spiked +3 light wooden shield that can grow a wall of thorns, as per the spell, once per day. This wall of thorns is 90 feet long and 10 feet thick and lasts 90 minutes. It must be created in a straight line and is not shapeable by the wielder. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, wall of thorns. [Dragon #328 (Bazaar of the Bizarre: Treasures of the Elven Empire)]
Shield of the Sun	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ShieldProfHeavy.Shield.Heavy.ShieldProf.Specific	PROFICIENCY:SHIELD|Shield (Heavy)	ACCHECK:-2	CRITMULT:x2	CRITRANGE:1	DAMAGE:1d4	WIELD:OneHanded	SIZE:M	SPELLFAILURE:15	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=Shield	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|2	COST:74170	WT:15	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=ShieldEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1426	SPROP:Aura Strong evocation; CL 13th; Slot –– (held); Activation –– and Standard (command); Item level 19	DESC:A heavy steel shield with a highly polished concave reflective surface that contains a large golden gem at its center. &nl;The Shield of the Sun is a +2 heavy steel shield. Twice per day, on command, the gem can ignite a brilliant beam of sunlight, blinding the living and destroying the undead. This effect is equivalent to a sunbeam spell (caster level 13th). &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, sunbeam. [Dragon #342 (Age of Worms: Wormfood – Surviving the Age of Worms Adventure Path – Forgotten Magic)]
Spiteful Imp	KEY:Spiteful Imp (DMC)	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ShieldProf.Shield.Buckler.ShieldProfBuckler.Specific	PROFICIENCY:SHIELD|Buckler	ACCHECK:-1	SPELLFAILURE:5	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1|TYPE=Shield	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|1	COST:46245	WT:3	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|4|TYPE=ShieldEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1426	SPROP:Aura Strong evocation, necromancy, and transmutation; CL 12th; Slot –– (held); Activation –– and Standard (command); Item level 17	DESC:A small mithral shield forged in the shape of an imp's face grinning in malicious glee. &nl;A +4 animated buckler. Once per day, the wearer can command it to spit burning venom. The venomous spittle requires a ranged touch attack at the wielder's ranged attack bonus. Its range is 30 feet, and it deals 1d4+6 points of fire damage. Like a poison spell, the venom also deals 1d10 points of Constitution damage (Fort DC 17 negates) and an additional 1d10 points of Constitution damage 1 minute later. The spiteful imp also has an unusual tendency to titter in evil mirth whenever it deflects an opponent's weapon-a disquieting but otherwise harmless quality. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, animate objects, poison, produce flame. [Dragon #312 (Rogues Gallery: The Heroes of the War of the Spider Queen Part II)]
Star Tortoise Shield	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ShieldProfHeavy.Shield.Heavy.ShieldProf.Specific	PROFICIENCY:SHIELD|Shield (Heavy)	ACCHECK:-2	CRITMULT:x2	CRITRANGE:1	DAMAGE:1d4	WIELD:OneHanded	SIZE:M	SPELLFAILURE:15	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=Shield	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|2	COST:18157	WT:12	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|3|TYPE=ShieldEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1426	SPROP:Aura Moderate abjuration; CL 9th; Slot –– (held); Item level 15	DESC:Lizardfolk make these large, oval shields out of the tough shells of tortoises. The shields are usually dark green, blue, or black with yellow or red patterns radiating out from the center like a starburst. &nl;The bearer of such a shield gains both its mundane defense but also some of the tortoise's natural defenses. A star tortoise shield is a +3 heavy wooden shield that also grants its bearer a +1 natural armor bonus. In addition, it renders its bearer immune to the decapitating ability of a vorpal weapon or similar effects. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor. [Dragon #335 (Bazaar of the Bizarre: Swamp Swag)]
Trueword Buckler	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ShieldProf.Shield.Buckler.ShieldProfBuckler.Specific	PROFICIENCY:SHIELD|Buckler	ACCHECK:-1	SPELLFAILURE:5	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1|TYPE=Shield	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|1	COST:27415	WT:3	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|4|TYPE=ShieldEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1426	SPROP:Aura Strong abjuration; CL 13th; Slot –– (held); Activation –– and Standard (command); Item level 16	DESC:To a follower of Torm, the True God, the item's material is immediately apparent; it is Torm's own skin. While the unenlightened sees only a leather clad buckler, a follower of Torm sees, burned into the flesh, the word "truth" written in ten different languages. &nl;The relic acts as a +4 darkwood buckler and grants the wearer two additional powers. Once per tenday, the wearer can discern lies, like the spell heightened to 5th level. A DC 17 Will save resists this effect. Additionally, the buckler can activate the spell hand of Torm presented in Magic of Faerûn once per day. A DC 16 Fortitude save resists this effect. Both effects are cast at 9th-level. &nl;Relic Power: To use this relic, you must worship Torm and either sacrifice a 5th-level divine spell slot or have the True Believer feat and at least 9 Hit Dice. At the DM's discretion, the Hit Die restriction can be lowered if you are one of the Martyr's Progeny. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Magic Arms and Armor, Sanctify Relic, discern lies, hand of Torm, creator must worship Torm. &nl;Lore: One of the greatest sacrifices in the Time of Troubles took place in the harbor of Tantras. Torm the True, bolstered to towering size, killed Bane-only to die himself from the struggle. His sacrifice was coupled with those of thousands of faithful, who willingly gave their lives so that Torm could prevail. Since the True One was restored to life by the overgod Ao, these shields have appeared on the forearms of the Martyr's Progeny, group of devout adolescents orphaned by the crisis in Tantras. [Dragon #333 (The Relics of Faerûn: Gifts From The Gods)]
Unholy Bloodshield	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ShieldProf.Shield.Buckler.ShieldProfBuckler.Specific.Relic	PROFICIENCY:SHIELD|Buckler	ACCHECK:-1	SPELLFAILURE:5	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1|TYPE=Shield	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|1	COST:0	WT:5	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|4|TYPE=ShieldEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1427	SPROP:Slot –– (held); Activation –– and Standard (command)	DESC:This buckler drips blood and trails gray energy whenever the wielder is angry or severely wounded. Its spikes are actually six iron arrows projecting through the metal of the shield (paralleling the design of Hextor's holy symbol). &nl;On command, this +4 mithral spiked buckler changes to a +4 mithral spiked light shield and the spikes gain the wounding property (the spikes are not useable unless in light shield form). The shield (in either form) counts as a holy symbol of Hextor for anyone who casts divine spells. &nl;Lore: For many years, this item was stored in the Battlehall of the Unholy Bloodshield in the palace at Rauxes (which was also the headquarters of the legion sharing the item's name), but it vanished around the time of the mysterious attack that ruined the capital. It has been missing ever since, with no signs or even any substantiated rumors placing it in the hands of anyone else. [Dragon #356 (Core Beliefs: Hextor)]
Unicorn's Shield	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.ShieldProfHeavy.Shield.Heavy.ShieldProf.Specific	PROFICIENCY:SHIELD|Shield (Heavy)	ACCHECK:-2	CRITMULT:x2	CRITRANGE:1	DAMAGE:1d4	WIELD:OneHanded	SIZE:M	SPELLFAILURE:15	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=Shield	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|2	COST:9170	WT:15	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2|TYPE=ShieldEnhancement	SOURCEPAGE:p.1427	SPROP:Aura Moderate transmutation; CL 6th; Slot –– (held); Activation –– and See text; Item level 12	DESC:This white heavy shield is emblazoned with the sign of a unicorn. &nl;The unicorn's shield is an adamantine +2 heavy shield and if it is used to make a shield bash attack as part of a charge, its true magical nature becomes apparent. The shield bestows an additional +2 bonus to AC for 1 round and the shield bash attack deals double normal damage. These benefits apply only during a charge. &nl;Prerequisites: Craft Wondrous Item, bull's strength, shield of faith. [Dragon #340 (Bazaar of the Bizarre: Items of the Zodiac)]
